# CODEOWNERS for cc-standards
#
# Review routing is a standards mechanism, not a courtesy: required reviews are enforced by
# branch protection, so an unowned change cannot merge (standards.md STD-REV-001).
#
# NOTE: this file must live at the repository root (or .github/) to be auto-detected. It is
# also extensionless, which some artifact stores drop -- the scaffold step copies it to
# each consuming repo as .github/CODEOWNERS, which is persisted and equally valid.
#
# Rules
#   - Every path in this repo must be owned. A fallback owner means an orphaned file is
#     still routed somewhere.
#   - Two-person review is required for the wire contract, conformance configs, CI, and
#     anything binding all four SDKs (standards.md STD-REV-003).
#   - Substitute real GitHub handles. Bracketed entries are role placeholders to be filled.

# ---- Global fallback: the cloud compute administrators ----
*                                    @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins

# ---- Layer 1: language-agnostic obligations ----
# Changing these changes what all 27 repos must do. Standard Owner approval is mandatory.
/standards.md                        @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins
/README.md                           @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins

# ---- Layer 2: style, per-language ----
# Language stewards own their toolchain and its version bumps. A bump is a minor release of
# the conformance pack and is never bundled with a feature change.
/styles.md                           @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins
/conformance/python/                 @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-python-steward
/conformance/java/                   @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-java-steward
/conformance/go/                     @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-go-steward
/conformance/dotnet/                 @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-dotnet-steward
/conformance/markdown/               @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins
/conformance/docker/                 @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins
/conformance/actions/                @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins

# ---- The wire contract: highest blast radius in the program ----
# All four SDK deserializers plus every registered plugin image depend on these fixtures.
# A fixture change here is functionally a contract change.
/contracts/                          @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins

# ---- CI: supply-chain security surface ----
# Workflow files decide what runs with which credentials. Security review is mandatory,
# because this is where STD-SEC-001/002 (no secrets in fork contexts) is implemented.
/ci/                                 @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins
/.github/workflows/                  @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins

# ---- Decisions ----
# An ADR is the only mechanism that can bind all four SDKs at once, and it is the program's
# audit trail for why a standard changed.
/adr/                                @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins

# ---- Templates consumed by 27 repos ----
/templates/                          @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins

# ---- Security and conduct documents ----
/SECURITY.md                         @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                  @USACE-Cloud-Compute/cc-admins

# ---- Exemptions: none ----
# An owned-by-nothing path is how an unreviewed change reaches main. Do not add wildcard
# exclusions to this file.
